/F1 9 Tf
(- No alert is not a clean bill of health. In Dechow, Sloan and Sweeney \(1995\), the most powerful) '
/F1 9 Tf
(  accruals model rejected 'no manipulation' for only 28.1% of 32 companies sanctioned by the SEC) '
/F1 9 Tf
(  \(Table 7, p. 32\).) '
/F1 9 Tf
(- In study 1, 49.9% of evaluated non-financial company-years \(48.3% including financial) '
/F1 9 Tf
(  companies\) were in alert, and the number of detections did not beat chance in a descriptive) '
/F1 9 Tf
(  test done after the result: 7 detections in 13 detectable cases, against 7.37 expected by) '
/F1 9 Tf
(  chance without assuming independent years \(8.56 assuming independent years\).) '
/F1 9 Tf
(- Risk models use numbers that may be manipulated \(Pereira and Martins 2015, p. 29\). That is why) '
/F1 9 Tf
(  the three families are not added up.) '
/F1 9 Tf
() '
/F2 11 Tf
